  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(x)$ be a second degree polynomial. If $f(1)=f(-1)$ and $p, q, r$ are in A.P., then $f^{\\prime}(p), f^{\\prime}(q), f^{\\prime}(r)$ are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
